      "reason": "Severe hypoglycaemia",
      "note": "Patient brought in by spouse after being found confused and diaphoretic at home. Field glucose 48 mg/dL. Treated with oral glucose gel and one ampoule of D50 with rapid resolution of symptoms. Patient reports he did not feel the usual warning symptoms before the episode and states this has happened three times since the autumn. Discharged home after two hours of observation with glucose 132 mg/dL. Endocrinology follow-up arranged. Impression: level 2 hypoglycaemia with impaired awareness on a multiple-daily-injection insulin regimen.",
